# tools/al/ales_notch_witness.rish — a band-reject (notch): keep the edges, drop the middle — the complement of ALES46's band-pass (ALES47).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES47.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-165728_fill-ales47-lotus-band-reject.md
# Stands on: lotus/tone.rye (ALES40 — low_pass, high_pass, precheck) and lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip and saturate); shape from lotus/shelf.rye (ALES41).
#
# lotus/notch.rye sums a low-pass (keeps the lows) and a high-pass (keeps the highs) in parallel, clamped once, so what neither
# branch keeps — the middle band between the cutoffs — is rejected. The selftest proves: silence stays silence; equal cutoffs are
# the identity (the reject band has zero width — low_pass + high_pass = x, the elegant crux); a constant input settles to itself
# (the notch keeps direct current — the exact contrast to the band-pass); a distinct-cutoff notch equals neither the input nor
# either single filter (a real middle band removed); a loud transient stays in range (the single i64 clamp); an illegal cutoff on
# either edge refuses BadCoeff, an out-of-range span BadRange. Purely local — no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no
# real sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_notch_witness.rish

say "ales-notch: Language EN — ALES47 sums ALES40's low-pass and high-pass in parallel to keep the edges and drop the middle, the complement of ALES46's band-pass — the gesture a keeper reaches for to remove a range (mains hum, a resonant ring, the mud) while the lows and the air stay whole."
say "ales-notch: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: equal cutoffs reconstruct the input byte-for-byte (a zero-width reject removes nothing), a constant settles to itself (the notch keeps direct current), and a distinct-cutoff notch genuinely removes a middle band."
say "ales-notch: Lens TAME — bounded Clip, u32 span, i16 samples, two scratch bands and the sum in i64 with a single clamp (ALES8's fader lesson); both cutoffs checked up front through tone.precheck before any scratch is filled; the notch adds no arithmetic on the audio path; an illegal cutoff on either edge refuses BadCoeff, an out-of-range span BadRange, each before a write; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/notch"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/notch.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-notch: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/notch.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-notch: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-notch: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-notch' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-notch: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-notch line"

# The band-pass and the band-reject are the EQ primitive pair — prove ALES46's band-pass still stands by its own green, so the pair is whole.
let band = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/band.rye -femit-bin=lotus/bin/band && lotus/bin/band selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-band' && echo yes"]
assert (trim band.out) == "yes" else "ales-notch: the ALES46 band-pass witness regressed under the band-reject"

say "ales-notch: GREEN — a band-reject keeps the edges and drops the middle by summing ALES40's low-pass and high-pass in parallel, clamped once; equal cutoffs reconstruct the input byte-for-byte (the elegant crux — a zero-width reject removes nothing), a constant settles to itself (the notch keeps direct current, the exact contrast to the band-pass), a distinct-cutoff notch equals neither the input nor either single filter, and a loud transient stays in range; an illegal cutoff on either edge refuses BadCoeff and an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving the clip untouched; the ALES46 band-pass selftest stays GREEN, so the band-pass/band-reject pair is whole. The next Lotus rung can carry the notch's cutoffs into a sweep, gain the retained bands (a parametric bell), or name the two edges in hertz through a real time base."
